                <p>Most recently at <b>Fortis Games</b>, I rewrote the player profile migration pipeline for <b>Twilight Towers</b> while the live game depended on it. I made the game simulation run headless so it could be unit tested for the first time, validated every change against thousands of real player profiles, and replaced the legacy code with a data-driven system that other engineers now use to ship migrations for their own features.</p>

                <p>As a Tools Programmer on <b>Havoc Crew</b>, <b>Southfield</b>, and <b>Star Citizen</b>, I built the authoring tools designers and artists used every day – from dungeon crawler room editing for level designers, to prop placement brushes and icon generation for artists. I gather requirements directly from the people who use what I build, iterate against their feedback, and record documentation and tutorials so it gets adopted.</p>

                <p>Throughout my career I have reviewed code, mentored developers, and taken owenership over the production processes. On <b>LEGO® Star Wars™ Battles</b>, I was Feature Lead for weekly leaderboards and clans, building each from the cloud services through to the client UI.</p>

                <p>I am at my best in a central, cross-disciplinary role, taking ownership of the systems others build on and helping the people around me do their best work.</p>

                <div class="spacer"></div>

                <p>Thank you for your consideration.</p>

                <p>Sincerely,</p>

